KSycoca: count symlinks along a resource path as modifications

The cache is declared valid while no resource directory's mtime exceeds the
stamp taken at build. On immutable package stores every such directory is a
symlink chain into a store whose mtimes are pinned (NixOS: epoch+1), so the
stamp never moves and a new generation is never noticed; the only invalidation
left is deleting the cache from outside, which a long-lived process with a
dead inotify watch never sees.

A path's modification time is now the newest of its final target and of every
symlink traversed while resolving it. Retargeting a link is a modification of
what the path names. Applied at the three stamp sites in KBuildSycoca and both
checks in TimestampChecker, so a stamp compares against itself and stays
stable once rebuilt.

